# Bringing it all together 🛡️

Now, protecting any endpoint is trivially easy! Just add the `get_current_user` dependency.

```python_not
@app.get("/secret-dashboard/")
def secret_data(current_user: str = Depends(get_current_user)):
    # If the user doesn't pass a valid token, this code NEVER runs.
    # FastAPI automatically blocks them with a 401 Unauthorized error.

    return {
        "message": f"Welcome to the secret area, {current_user}!",
        "bank_balance": 1000000
    }
```

# Enforcing Permissions ⛔

Now, when you protect a route, you can declare exactly which scopes are required using `Security()` instead of `Depends()`.

```python_not
from fastapi import Security

# Only users whose JWT contains the 'admin' scope can access this!
@app.get("/admin/dashboard")
def get_admin_data(current_user: User = Security(get_current_user, scopes=["admin"])):
    return {"secret_data": "You are an admin!"}
```
FastAPI automatically checks the scopes list inside the JWT. If the user doesn't have the `"admin"` scope, FastAPI returns a 403 Forbidden error!
